# Heratio DEV: hourly facet-cache refresh for /usr/share/nginx/heratio-dev.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Two other things refresh facets, and neither covers dev:
#
#   - /etc/cron.d/ahg-facet-cache iterates `for d in dam heratio` only, and runs
#     the PROD codebase (/usr/share/nginx/heratio/artisan) with a DB_DATABASE
#     override. Pointing that at heratio_dev would run prod's code against dev's
#     database - exactly the cross-wiring to avoid while dev is mid-development.
#   - The managed cron_schedule row `refresh-facet-cache` is driven by Laravel's
#     scheduler, and dev's scheduler is deliberately disabled
#     (/etc/cron.d/heratio-dev-schedule.disabled), so the row never fires here
#     whatever its is_enabled value.
#
# The result was dev facets going 66 hours stale (found 2026-08-18), which makes
# browse/facet behaviour on dev quietly unlike prod while testing it.
#
# Same pattern as /etc/cron.d/heratio-am-dev: dev's scheduler stays off, and the
# individual commands dev genuinely needs get their own entry here, running DEV's
# OWN artisan so they use dev's .env, database and uploads paths.
#
# Run as www-data (never root: artisan bootstrap would create root-owned logs
# that the worker can then no longer write). Absolute paths to php and artisan
# because /etc/cron.d/* commands run with cwd=/.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
MAILTO=""
0 * * * * www-data flock -n /run/lock/heratio-dev-facet-cache.lock -c '/usr/bin/php8.3 /usr/share/nginx/heratio-dev/artisan ahg:refresh-facet-cache >> /var/log/heratio-dev-facet-cache.log 2>&1'
